language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Diet problem: choose how many units of each of four foods to buy so that each nutrient reaches its minimum requirement, at the lowest cost. Foods are chocolate cake, chocolate ice cream, cola and pineapple cheesecake.
given price : matrix indexed by [int(1..4)] of int(0..)
given limits : matrix indexed by [int(1..4)] of int(0..)
find units : matrix indexed by [int(1..4)] of int(0..50)
find cost : int(0..10000)

minimising cost

such that
$ the nutrient content of each food per unit, rows are calories, chocolate, sugar and fat, columns are the four foods
$ the total cost is the price of the units bought
cost = (sum i : int(1..4) . price[i] * units[i]),
$ calories: at least the required amount
(sum i : int(1..4) . [400, 200, 150, 500][i] * units[i]) >= limits[1],
$ chocolate (ounces): at least the required amount
(sum i : int(1..4) . [3, 2, 0, 0][i] * units[i]) >= limits[2],
$ sugar (ounces): at least the required amount
(sum i : int(1..4) . [2, 2, 4, 4][i] * units[i]) >= limits[3],
$ fat (ounces): at least the required amount
(sum i : int(1..4) . [2, 4, 1, 5][i] * units[i]) >= limits[4]
